.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt ISEQSIG 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm iseqsig
.Nd "signaling floating-point equality comparison"
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libm
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In math.h
.Ft int
.Fn iseqsig "real-floating x" "real-floating y"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn iseqsig
macro determines whether its arguments are equal.
Arguments of different types are compared as by the
.Li ==
operator, after the usual arithmetic conversions.
Positive and negative zero compare equal.
.Pp
Unlike the equality operator, which is a quiet comparison,
.Fn iseqsig
raises the
.Dv FE_INVALID
floating-point exception if either argument is a NaN, quiet or
signaling, considered a domain error.
As
.Va math_errhandling
is
.Dv MATH_ERREXCEPT ,
.Va errno
is not set.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn iseqsig
macro returns 1 if its arguments are equal and 0 otherwise.
If either argument is a NaN, it returns 0.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fenv 3 ,
.Xr isgreater 3 ,
.Xr math 3
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn iseqsig
macro conforms to
.St -isoC-2023 .
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn iseqsig
macro first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
